From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] synth: a partition reads its blackbox list from a file
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A partition of a parallel synthesis took the modules to blackbox in
SYNTH_BLACKBOXES, one environment variable. Linux caps one environment
string at 128 KiB (MAX_ARG_STRLEN): XiangShan's XSTile with 2,250 kept
modules is 206 KB of names, and starting synthesis failed with
"Argument list too long" on every partition. The list can now come in
SYNTH_BLACKBOXES_FILE, one name per line, as bazel-orfs's
synth_partition.sh writes it; SYNTH_BLACKBOXES still works.

Upstream as The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD-flow-scripts#4798; retires at
a //:bump onto an ORFS that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
diff --git a/flow/scripts/synth.tcl b/flow/scripts/synth.tcl
index 59557c92f..683e73f43 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/synth.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/synth.tcl
@@ -58,10 +58,22 @@ if { [env_var_exists_and_non_empty SYNTH_CHECKPOINT] } {
 #     the checkpoint.  In synth_preamble.tcl a single design is being
 #     synthesised, so an unknown name is almost certainly a user typo and
 #     should fail loudly — `blackbox $m` without `catch` is intentional.
-if { [env_var_exists_and_non_empty SYNTH_BLACKBOXES] } {
-  foreach m $::env(SYNTH_BLACKBOXES) {
-    catch { blackbox $m }
+#
+# An orchestrator with thousands of kept modules gives the list in a file
+# instead, SYNTH_BLACKBOXES_FILE, one name per line: Linux caps one
+# environment string at 128 KiB, and 2,250 names are 206 KB.
+set synth_blackboxes [env_var_or_empty SYNTH_BLACKBOXES]
+if { [env_var_exists_and_non_empty SYNTH_BLACKBOXES_FILE] } {
+  set fid [open $::env(SYNTH_BLACKBOXES_FILE) r]
+  foreach m [split [read $fid] "\n"] {
+    if { $m ne "" } {
+      lappend synth_blackboxes $m
+    }
   }
+  close $fid
+}
+foreach m $synth_blackboxes {
+  catch { blackbox $m }
 }
 
 hierarchy -check -top $::env(DESIGN_NAME)
